            <ArticleTitle>Interstitial cystitis and endometriosis in a 12-year-old girl.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>115-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00404-010-1808-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Interstitial cystitis (IC) is a common cause of pelvic pain in the general female population and is thought to be understated in young female patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 12-year-old girl with IC and endometriosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">A single case report.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">It is important to screen for IC in young patients with endometriosis and vice versa.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
